========================

Biorouter's installers and packages redistribute the components below. Each
one's own licence text ships with it at the path named here. This file is a
summary, not a substitute for those texts.


Open Computer Use
-----------------
  Used for:  the native desktop helper behind Biorouter Copilot
  Licence:   MIT
  Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 Leo
  Upstream:  https://github.com/iFurySt/open-codex-computer-use
  Version:   0.3.5, pinned at commit 547b4ffb8ed731a8f16486e6d8a3b215484267d3
  Licence text and notice:
    in this repository   vendor/computer-use/{LICENSE,NOTICE}
    in an installed app  beside the helper binary, inside the payload

  The upstream source is vendored in full at vendor/computer-use/source, so a
  build needs no network. Biorouter's own changes are kept separately in
  vendor/computer-use/patches and are applied to a throwaway copy at build
  time, never to the vendored tree.

  The build copies LICENSE and NOTICE into the shipped payload and records
  their checksums in the payload manifest, and the verify step fails the build
  if the manifest and the files on disk disagree. The notice cannot be dropped
  by a packaging change without the build noticing.

  Upstream's extracted cursor artwork is deliberately not vendored and not
  distributed. It was extracted from another vendor's shipped application, and
  MIT covers upstream's own work rather than somebody else's artwork. The
  cursor Biorouter ships is drawn procedurally by its own build script.


